WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.440
<i>One of the greatest wrestlers of all time</i>

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.560
<i>just got sucker punched.</i>

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.400
<i>When you see the words
"Hulk Hogan sex tape,"</i>

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.760
you have that moment before you decide
whether or not to click it.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.160
Hogan's $100 million lawsuit

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.720
<i>over a tape that was posted online
by the website </i> Gawker.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.200
<i>It's the first celebrity sex tape case
to go to trial.</i>

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.920
<i>It put Internet privacy</i>

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.640
<i>in a battle against freedom of the press.</i>

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.680
<i>Gawker </i> becomes convinced
that somebody with a different agenda

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.760
<i>is financing this lawsuit.</i>

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.280
Billionaire Peter Thiel,
a co-founder of PayPal,

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.840
<i>is secretly paying the expenses
of Hulk Hogan's legal fight.</i>

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.400
A story about his sexual orientation was
published nine years before this lawsuit.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.440
<i>This is personal.</i>

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.240
<i>He's doing this
because he wants to bring </i> Gawker<i>  down.</i>

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.360
We're gonna open up those libel laws,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.880
<i>and we're going to have people sue you
like you never got sued before.</i>

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.680
<i>Donald Trump, Peter Thiel,
and other billionaires...</i>

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.880
have tried to undercut freedom of speech.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.360
Sheldon Adelson bought
the <i> Las Vegas Review-Journal.</i>

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.040
<i>What he did was take off the boards</i>

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.080
people who might reveal something
that he doesn't like.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.280
Billionaires are proclaiming,
"We are more powerful than the truth."

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.560
This is a moment of real definition
for the press.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.400
You are fake news.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.600
<i>Journalism is worth protecting.</i>

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:29.040
<i>If we lose that,
we've lost what America stands for.</i>

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.560
We have to fight harder
and smarter than ever.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.920
<i>Here's a message to the White House:</i>

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.040
<i>you keep lying,
we're going to keep reporting.</i>

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.360
<i>The president believes the press
is a threat to the country.</i>

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:41.080
-<i> Alternative facts are not facts.
- He thinks democracy is outmoded.</i>

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.320
<i>Money can't silence the media.</i>

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.920
<i>-We're talking about the truth.
-Can you turn the microphone off?</i>

